   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Food security and income-generating support delivered to poor and vulnerable women 
Indicator: At least 250 poor and vulnerable households headed by women received backyard gardening support and training in crop management, food preparation, and nutrition 
Progress/Status: 1a. In Port Vila, 60 beneficiaries received backyard gardening training; 60 beneficiaries received nutrition training; and 98 beneficiaries received complete backyard gardening set-up. 75 households have harvested. 

In Luganville, 107 beneficiaries received backyard gardening training; 82 beneficiaries received nutrition training; and 107 beneficiaries have received complete backyard gardening set-up.

On track. Completion of backyard gardening training and nutrition training for 90 beneficiaries in Port Vila is targeted by December 2025. 52 remaining beneficiaries are targeted to receive complete backyard gardening setup.

Remaining 18 beneficiaries in Luganville will be trained by May 2026. 75% of the beneficiaries have harvested. 
Data Source: PST quarterly project progress report; pre- and post-training report; M&amp;E firm&amp;apos;s baseline, midline, and endpoint evaluation; and ADB project missions 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
