    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Food security and income-generating support delivered to poor and vulnerable women 
Indicator: At least 250 poor and vulnerable women received food processing training and coaching on microbusiness development and management 
Progress/Status: In Port Vila, a total of 161 participated in the Food Safety Training of which 139 are from the beneficiary list; 159 participated in Food Processing Training, of which 132 are from the original beneficiary list; and 146 in the Business Entrepreneurship Training of which 97 are from the original beneficiary list.  

In Luganville, there were 171 participants in the Food Safety Training, of which 97 are from the beneficiary list and 91 participants in the Business Entrepreneurship training.  

On Track. Food Processing Training for 120 -150 participants Luganville is targeted for completion by 31 October 2025 (4-5 sessions). Additional training for food safety in Port Vila and Luganville is targeted by October and November 2025, respectively, and additional food processing training in Port Vila is targeted by November 2025. 
